# BUGS

`malloc` and its kin do not set `errno` when they fail, and `free` of a pointer not from the heap traps.
Memory from small blocks is never returned to the system.

`<stdlib.h>` has no `system`, `rand`, `srand`, `setenv`, `unsetenv`, `putenv`, `mblen`, `wctomb` and the like, `strtol_l`, `at_quick_exit` or `quick_exit`.

A program built without the file library (rather than with fdio, which has the file calls of this page) finds `realpath` and `mktemp` failing with `ENOENT`, and `mkstemp` not defined.
